From e708526f1894979e91716a6ab53aa67eeadcf2f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Tada Antunes <leonardotada@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:08:11 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Run every finalizer of a cycle before any dead slot is
 released

The sweep used to finalize slab by slab and put each swept slab back in its
bin at once, so a finalizer that read another dead object (it works with a
collector that frees nothing until the end, and programs rely on it) could
find that object's slot reused, or poisoned. A finalize pass over all blocks now
comes first; the release passes follow. Mutators that help with the sweep
leave the finalize pass to the sweeper and wait without taking the lock.

A slab remembers that a slot of it ever got a finalizer, and the pass skips the
others without touching their slots; with no finalizer anywhere it is skipped.
Sweep serials are 16 bits now: gcCycle + 1 wrapped to 0 at cycle 255, and 0
is the value of a block no sweep has seen.

finalizer_order.d: 2000 to 285000 damaged partners per run before, none after.
Cost: alloc with 8 threads about 12% (the pass walks the blocks).
